WEBVTT

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:30.000
- Hey, brother. How are you doing? - Okay, man.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.370
It's not something that belonged to me.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.570
I would like to have it back.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.500
Look what jumped out of your pocket, brother.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.930
Looks like pure shit to me.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:58.450
Hold it.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:02:59.670
Don't you ever touch me, man.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:33.560
Come on.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:27.360
- Do you speak English? - Yes, ma'am.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:29.220
Take me to Joe's Haven.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.560
Uh-uh. No taxis go to Yellow Section.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.520
It's Hong Kong's no-man's land.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:37.910
Only criminals and gangsters live there.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.680
Even police are afraid to go there.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.760
Well, I'm going there. Can you take me?

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.100
Well, I'll take you up to where it's safe, all right?

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.100
Okay, let's go.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:08.230
- I stop here. It's not safe to go anymore. - Which way do I go from here?

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.750
- The address you seek is over there. - Thank you.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.600
Good job.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:29.220
Ich muss mich aber wundern, was sagt man sich an der Busfahrer.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:35.770
Do you speak English?

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:39.130
I don't know.

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:41.110
Do you know this address?

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:44.360
I don't know.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:51.600
I don't know.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:09.190
Come on fellas, I ain't looking for no trouble.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:49.270
Back up.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.420
Thanks, but there's nothing I couldn't handle.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.460
What are you doing in this part of town?

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.200
I'm looking for a place called Joe's Haven.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.750
Do you know where it is?

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.290
Yeah, I know where it is.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:14.170
Come on, I'll drop you.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:17.940
I'm Elaine.

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:19.830
- Are you new around here? - Yeah.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:24.090
- Business with Joe? - I don't even know him.

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:26.330
You planning on staying around for a long time?

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.140
Look, lady, or whoever you are,

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.000
I accepted a ride from you to Joe's Haven.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.970
and that's all you need to know about me, bitch.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:36.560
Let me give you a little piece of friendly advice.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:39.230
Take care of your business and then get out of here.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:42.160
You know, this isn't exactly a safe place for Green Road.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.370
You seem to get around pretty good.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.320
Yeah, well, I know the right people.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:47.860
Yeah, I can imagine.

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:11.230
Can I help you?

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:14.400
I'm looking for Joe.

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:32.830
- What can I do for you?

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.570
- You can take me to see Joe, that's what you can do for me.

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:36.810
- Well, I'm Joe.

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:40.360
- You're putting me on.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:42.500
Who ever heard of a Chinaman named Joe?

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.620
- Well, I'm only Chinese and buddy,

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:46.440
but my mind is Western.

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:48.150
That's why everybody calls me Joe.

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:54.380
- They call me TNT.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.910
I'm looking for a friend I think you might be able

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:58.170
to help me find.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:00.000
- I know everybody around me.

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:06.510
Do you know him?

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:09.480
Come on, Joe, his name is Stack Jackson.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.230
He sent me your address asking me to send him some money.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.420
Instead, I sent him for peace of my mind.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:21.270
I just want to know if he got it.

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:26.790
He never came for it.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:28.510
What do you think happened to him?

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:30.000
A lot of guys come and go in this neighborhood.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:34.840
- Don't poke any.

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:43.270
- Jackson, I'm back.

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:46.450
- Excuse me.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.960
不必跑

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:33.110
Come on.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:28.450
- I'm impressed, it's not bad.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.290
- You think you could do better?

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:34.910
- Yeah, I know I can do better.

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:38.890
So look, I think you're a fantastic lady.

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.130
What's your line?

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:43.470
- You name it, I do it.

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:45.610
- What brings you to this neighborhood?

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.330
- Got you guessing, don't I?

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:48.570
- Not for long.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.250
I got a way of getting in the middle of things,

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:51.960
sooner or later.

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:54.940
- Sounds interesting, but I can save you the hard labor.

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:55.880
I'm here looking for--

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:57.340
- A job.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:59.370
She's working for me.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:00.000
- You don't expect that?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.930
- You expect me to buy that, do you?

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:04.370
- You got a better offer?

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:08.460
- Yeah, maybe, it all depends on what you're after.

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:13.230
- Okay, I heard that anybody with guts and talent

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:16.000
could pick up some easy bread around here.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:21.260
I don't care what I have to do, just so long as it pays well.

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:25.130
- If you're on the real side, I'll keep an eye open for you.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:27.440
I may be able to do you some good after all.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.800
- Don't do me any favors.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:42.060
Maybe I don't do favors, and when I give, I get.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.910
- Who is he?

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:45.740
- Charlie.

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:47.400
Is there your vodka?

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:50.960
Nothing but trouble.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.800
- They're inside waiting.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.110
Did you find her?

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:57.560
- Yeah, she's an incredible lady.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.830
No problem though, she's a loner.

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:04.330
- Not likely she's working for anybody but herself.

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:06.440
- Are you sure?

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.550
- Baby, I'm always sure.

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:12.440
- Yeah, guess that's the problem.

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:15.040
- All right, what are you trying to say?

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:16.520
- I'm just wondering if Sid and Ming

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:18.380
really appreciate your talents.

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:19.880
- Don't kid yourself.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:22.090
Sid knows exactly what I'm worth.

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:24.620
And who gives a fuck what that chink thinks?

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:26.190
- Your friend is stuck.

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:27.740
You really want to find him, huh?

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:28.990
- That's why I'm here.

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:30.000
- Better watch your step.

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:31.690
You do not know what he was into?

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:33.510
That's cool.

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:36.390
I just sit on my ass and expect Zach to come to me.

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:38.790
I look around and see what I can find out.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:43.050
Do you think you can get me an answer by next week?

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:47.740
It is possible, but they will insist on cash for every delivery.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:50.090
Hell, that's no problem.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:53.840
I'll pay hard cash for raw heroin any day at those prices.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:57.240
Do you want to hear what Charlie has to say?

00:16:57.460 --> 00:16:58.260
Yeah, what is it?

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:00.000
I checked out the lady.

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:03.430
And I can't see what she'd cause any trouble.

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:05.020
That's fine.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:05.900
Man, you better get moving.

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:12.560
I want an answer as soon as possible.

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:16.900
We have had no trouble for the past six months.

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:20.200
Let us not take any more risks at this point.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:25.230
I said I can't see it.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:26.810
- Do you need time out?

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.080
- Time.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:28.680
- Don't check.

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:34.690
- Are you the manager? - Yes, I am.

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:36.220
I need some information.

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:37.790
If I could be of any help.

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.380
I'm investigating

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:42.040
about the disappearance of a black American

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:45.090
by the name of Stack Jackson.

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:46.360
I don't know the name.

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:50.340
I was told that he was last seen here.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.010
Hey, wait.

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:53.510
There was a black man.

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:56.150
He was murdered here right on stage some weeks ago.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:04.580
No!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:59.190
How are you doing?

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:00.950
- Thank you.

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:08.740
- Okay, you are now looking at the biggest man

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:10.510
in the whole yellow district.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:13.110
They control all the rackets around.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:14.950
- You working on their protection?

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:18.320
- Uh-uh, we have an understanding.

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:20.200
I don't meddle on the operation.

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.080
They don't touch me.

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:25.120
- This could turn into an interesting evening.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:39.710
Hey, baby. Come on, get off your ass. I got some people who want to take a look at you, okay?

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:45.910
I don't operate that way. If they want to see me, they come to me. I don't go to anybody.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:49.470
Yeah, that sounds good, but they ain't gonna dig it.

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:53.240
I don't care if they don't dig it. I'm just telling you like it is.

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:56.620
- You know something? - What?

00:20:57.390 --> 00:20:58.930
I love your style.

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:03.520
Okay, let's forget about that.

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:05.910
Do it for me.

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:26.620
Sid, this is TNT.

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:29.380
Elaine, you've met.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.440
And that's me.

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:16.040
It looks like you're giving me some competition.

00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:19.290
Oh no, baby, not me.

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:23.810
Listen, honey, and you get it straight.

00:22:23.810 --> 00:22:26.160
I'm not in your league.

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:28.960
I work standing up, not on my back.

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:34.020
Really? How amusing. I've never really tried it that way.

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:40.700
Relax, honey. I'm not after your slot.

00:22:40.870 --> 00:22:44.330
I wasn't worried. You don't have what it takes.

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:49.420
Oh, I don't know about that. As long as it doesn't rub off.

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:52.150
Fuck you.

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:59.000
You shouldn't have done that.

00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:04.730
What do you expect? Congratulations for bumping heads with the man.

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:27.560
The door is open. I blew it, didn't I?

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:32.760
- That's what you call an understatement.

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:35.770
- How bad?

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:40.010
- I suggest you finish your butt

00:23:40.010 --> 00:23:41.650
and forget about your friend.

00:23:41.650 --> 00:23:43.350
Split before you end up like a...

00:23:43.350 --> 00:23:45.700
- Stack?

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:48.630
He's dead, isn't he?

00:23:48.630 --> 00:23:52.540
- What are you going to do now?

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:54.940
- I'm gonna get him, Joe.

00:23:54.940 --> 00:23:58.770
Whoever is responsible.

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:00.000
I'm gonna...

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.920
find him, and I'm going to bust

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:03.260
the motherfuckers to pieces.

00:24:04.700 --> 00:24:06.240
He was more than just a friend.

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:07.650
My brother.

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:14.140
What's going to happen with her?

00:24:14.900 --> 00:24:16.500
Well, Ming wants to run her out of town.

00:24:16.810 --> 00:24:18.350
But Charlie thinks she could be useful

00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:18.850
to us.

00:24:19.410 --> 00:24:22.520
You know, I just can't figure out what she's after.

00:24:22.660 --> 00:24:24.600
Do you think she knows that you're in the heroin business?

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:26.530
I'm not sure yet, but

00:24:26.530 --> 00:24:27.790
I'll find out.

00:24:28.800 --> 00:24:30.000
There's too much competition.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:35.010
around here can't you get rid of her and Ming and Charlie too in theory yes but I

00:24:35.010 --> 00:24:39.170
need Ming's contacts to get the heroin out of China I need Charlie to keep an

00:24:39.170 --> 00:24:43.130
eye on Ming and the black chick might come in handy what's gonna happen to her

00:24:43.130 --> 00:24:47.360
well still me for the time being Charlie's gonna keep an eye on her and

00:24:47.360 --> 00:24:51.000
Ming's going ahead with the next shipment this is the big one

00:25:37.390 --> 00:25:38.960
Let's go.

00:26:29.340 --> 00:26:30.000
trace of who

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:33.680
Yeah, well, I'm out a million bucks unless we recover that lost shipment.

00:26:33.680 --> 00:26:35.790
Got any ideas?

00:26:35.790 --> 00:26:39.130
I believe the black woman might have some knowledge of this.

00:26:39.130 --> 00:26:41.380
Well, it's possible.

00:26:41.380 --> 00:26:43.340
Anything's worth a try at this point.

00:26:43.340 --> 00:26:44.740
I'll have Charlie check it out.

00:26:44.740 --> 00:26:46.740
Perhaps I would be better qualified than Charlie.

00:26:46.740 --> 00:26:49.220
Better qualified to do what, Ming?

00:26:49.220 --> 00:26:57.170
It seems that your tolerance of the black woman was a costly mistake.

00:26:57.170 --> 00:27:00.000
What kind of shit is that?

00:27:00.220 --> 00:27:01.360
The Sherman was hijacked.

00:27:01.420 --> 00:27:02.000
Yeah, I'm hip.

00:27:03.190 --> 00:27:05.570
What I want to know is, why is Ming so quick to accuse T?

00:27:05.940 --> 00:27:08.360
As you two are very quick to proclaim her innocent.

00:27:09.330 --> 00:27:11.130
Perhaps you place too much emphasis on color.

00:27:11.770 --> 00:27:14.410
Or could it be that you know something more than you're willing to tell?

00:27:14.840 --> 00:27:17.780
No, but I got some pretty good ideas.

00:27:18.150 --> 00:27:20.150
Perhaps you would be kind enough to enlighten us.

00:27:20.490 --> 00:27:22.210
I think it had to be an inside job.

00:27:22.210 --> 00:27:26.890
Or how else would the hijackers have known where to set up an ambush?

00:27:27.800 --> 00:27:30.000
And why would they kill every witch?

00:27:31.280 --> 00:27:35.620
I choose not to defend my honor at this point.

00:27:35.620 --> 00:27:37.250
You have no choice but to trust me

00:27:37.250 --> 00:27:39.250
if you're to continue purchasing for my contact.

00:27:39.250 --> 00:27:41.550
Surely you're not planning on risking another shipment

00:27:41.550 --> 00:27:43.130
until you find out what happened.

00:27:43.130 --> 00:27:44.680
I got a quarter to meet.

00:27:44.680 --> 00:27:45.720
I'm open to suggestion.

00:27:45.720 --> 00:27:49.660
No, that's good, 'cause I got one.

00:27:49.660 --> 00:27:51.180
I won't in on the next delivery.

00:27:51.180 --> 00:27:52.760
Wonderful.

00:27:52.760 --> 00:27:54.660
Then you can share the blame if anything goes wrong.

00:27:54.660 --> 00:27:56.430
I'll do you one better.

00:27:56.430 --> 00:28:00.000
I'll take full responsibility, but I want to pick

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:04.960
I want to form a squad of the finest fighters in this city.

00:28:04.960 --> 00:28:06.980
This is agreeable to me.

00:28:06.980 --> 00:28:10.770
Good. Then it's settled.

00:28:36.360 --> 00:28:39.160
There have been some new developments. You better alert your people.

00:28:39.350 --> 00:28:42.130
- Any idea when? - No, I think we can hit the next shipment.

00:28:42.290 --> 00:28:44.730
- Where? - I'll let you know.

00:28:44.890 --> 00:28:48.020
- Where's everybody? - They went to see Charlie about the job.

00:28:49.450 --> 00:28:54.360
- Job? What kind of a job? - It seems that the last shipment of drag was hijacked.

00:28:54.840 --> 00:28:57.810
That's why Charlie is organizing some sort of a war party.

00:28:57.870 --> 00:29:00.000
Just to make sure it won't happen again.

00:29:00.480 --> 00:29:01.710
Sounds interesting.

00:29:01.710 --> 00:29:02.940
What do you think?

00:29:02.940 --> 00:29:03.940
Maybe I can join up.

00:29:03.940 --> 00:29:05.180
Huh?

00:29:05.180 --> 00:29:06.180
Are you crazy?

00:29:06.180 --> 00:29:09.570
What do you want to do that for?

00:29:09.570 --> 00:29:10.570
Come on, Joe.

00:29:10.570 --> 00:29:11.570
I'm no near a fire now.

00:29:11.570 --> 00:29:13.570
What happened to Stacked in the day I arrived here?

00:29:13.570 --> 00:29:16.430
Maybe if I get on the action, I might be able to find out a thing or two.

00:29:16.430 --> 00:29:17.440
Forget it, doll.

00:29:17.440 --> 00:29:18.440
It means trouble.

00:29:18.440 --> 00:29:19.440
You gonna take me or not?

00:29:19.440 --> 00:29:20.440
Uh-oh.

00:29:20.440 --> 00:29:21.260
Calm me out.

00:29:21.260 --> 00:29:22.400
I'm sorry.

00:29:22.400 --> 00:29:23.400
Excuse me.

00:29:23.400 --> 00:29:24.960
Don't you?

00:29:24.960 --> 00:29:29.630
Well, I'm just gonna have to find my own way.

00:29:33.230 --> 00:29:34.550
No many hours to change it.

00:29:35.660 --> 00:29:53.350
You got the men ready?

00:29:53.630 --> 00:29:53.950
Yes.

00:29:54.420 --> 00:29:54.720
How many?

00:29:55.350 --> 00:29:55.890
Ten men.

00:29:56.450 --> 00:29:57.730
Twelve counting you and me.

00:29:57.990 --> 00:29:58.770
That should do it.

00:30:14.330 --> 00:30:16.450
- Lady, you're full of surprises.

00:30:16.450 --> 00:30:17.730
How'd you get in here?

00:30:17.730 --> 00:30:18.870
- Ask them.

00:30:23.740 --> 00:30:26.720
- What do you want here?

00:30:26.720 --> 00:30:28.280
- That's the word you were hiring.

00:30:28.280 --> 00:30:30.000
I assumed it was an equal opportunity

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:34.940
Unemployment it you want to try that again. I want a spot in a new group you're forming

00:30:35.080 --> 00:30:41.930
Where did you hear that? That's not important. I want to know. I'm not telling you. It was Joe wasn't it?

00:30:42.030 --> 00:30:46.350
He's not involved. I came here for action and not talk. I don't dig it

00:30:46.470 --> 00:30:50.720
Why you want to get involved? A chick's gotta start from somewhere and fighting the thing I do best

00:30:51.310 --> 00:30:56.320
Different it's way out of your league. Try me. That's all I'm asking. Now, how am I supposed to do that?

00:30:56.580 --> 00:30:58.520
Let me fight your top man

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:02.740
No way.

00:31:02.740 --> 00:31:07.180
I'm not leaving until you give me a chance to show my stuff.

00:31:07.180 --> 00:31:09.040
Okay.

00:31:09.040 --> 00:31:13.640
You show me your stuff, then you split, all right?

00:31:48.400 --> 00:31:49.860
- This is what you wanted, huh?

00:31:49.860 --> 00:31:51.660
- I said, your best fighter.

00:31:51.660 --> 00:31:52.500
- You got it, man.

00:32:26.330 --> 00:32:27.760
Do I get the slot?

00:32:27.760 --> 00:32:30.000
Let's have a drink.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:30.700
and talk it over.

00:32:32.370 --> 00:32:35.700
You didn't say the drinks were going to be in your pad.

00:32:36.970 --> 00:32:39.460
Why don't you tell me what you're really after, huh?

00:32:40.120 --> 00:32:42.810
Just looking to pay my own way, that's all.

00:32:43.520 --> 00:32:45.300
You're too fine for all that fighting.

00:32:46.190 --> 00:32:47.570
Where'd you learn to fight like that?

00:32:48.700 --> 00:32:52.760
When I was a kid, one of my mother's boyfriends

00:32:52.760 --> 00:32:53.620
was a black belt.

00:32:54.520 --> 00:32:56.420
He taught me how to take care of myself.

00:32:57.600 --> 00:33:00.000
Don't you think it's about time you changed your methods?

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.510
A lady don't need to know how to fight.

00:33:02.510 --> 00:33:07.550
I haven't found a dude yet that can afford to pay the price.

00:33:07.550 --> 00:33:12.830
I don't mind paying for something, if it's worth it.

00:33:12.830 --> 00:33:15.330
What's on your squad, is that the price?

00:33:15.330 --> 00:33:21.420
I wouldn't waste your time with shit like that, talking about something big.

00:33:21.420 --> 00:33:23.560
I'm listening.

00:33:23.560 --> 00:33:26.760
How do I know you can handle it?

00:33:26.760 --> 00:33:29.700
You don't.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:38.550
- If you're serious. - Drink to that.

00:33:38.550 --> 00:33:45.320
That's as good as any man I've ever seen.

00:33:45.320 --> 00:33:49.260
So what are you suggesting?

00:33:49.260 --> 00:33:50.150
She should be eliminated.

00:33:50.150 --> 00:33:51.150
Now, wait a minute.

00:33:51.150 --> 00:33:54.170
You get rid of her, they're gonna send in someone else to take her place.

00:33:54.170 --> 00:33:55.170
Then where are you?

00:33:55.170 --> 00:33:56.170
Yeah, I think you're right.

00:33:56.170 --> 00:33:59.450
Give her a rope till she's done.

00:33:59.450 --> 00:34:00.000
Give her a rope till she's done.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:03.840
She hangs herself, along with whoever she's working for.

00:34:03.840 --> 00:34:07.010
Joe, I really need your help.

00:34:07.010 --> 00:34:11.600
When Charlie's men move out, I want to be around.

00:34:11.600 --> 00:34:14.810
Uh-uh. That's something you have to work out with Charlie.

00:34:14.810 --> 00:34:19.390
Not necessarily. Did you ever hear of a thing called spying?

00:34:19.390 --> 00:34:21.970
Hear of it? I invented it.

00:34:21.970 --> 00:34:25.530
All you got to do is find out when they move,

00:34:25.530 --> 00:34:29.040
and I just tag along and see what happens.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.490
- You got a head like a rock.

00:34:32.490 --> 00:34:34.890
You'll never get away with it.

00:34:34.890 --> 00:34:37.290
- The answer is no, and oh no.

00:34:37.290 --> 00:34:41.380
- I promise I won't do anything foolish.

00:34:41.380 --> 00:34:45.350
- Well, in that case, it's your funeral.

00:34:45.350 --> 00:34:52.390
Charlie is meeting the children in the cemetery.

00:34:52.390 --> 00:34:55.190
- Let's do it.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:30.740
Come on.

00:38:39.020 --> 00:38:41.270
- This is trouble, but trouble.

00:39:00.350 --> 00:39:05.090
- All right, what happened?

00:39:05.090 --> 00:39:08.330
- They got us, right after the exchange.

00:39:08.330 --> 00:39:09.960
- Who?

00:39:09.960 --> 00:39:13.320
- I don't know, I never saw them before.

00:39:13.320 --> 00:39:18.590
- Great, just great.

00:39:18.590 --> 00:39:20.050
You wanted to handle the delivery,

00:39:20.050 --> 00:39:23.850
assumed full responsibility, and now you've blown it.

00:39:23.850 --> 00:39:26.070
Have you got any more ideas, bright boy?

00:39:26.070 --> 00:39:27.910
- Perhaps after this unfortunate incident

00:39:27.910 --> 00:39:30.000
you would be kind enough to allow us a confrontation.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:34.010
If it makes you happy, I'll say she has nothing to do with it.

00:39:34.010 --> 00:39:37.330
I once know a magician that could make people disappear.

00:39:37.330 --> 00:39:41.300
It's gonna take more than magic.

00:39:41.300 --> 00:39:43.300
Oh, no, you're not thinking of...

00:39:43.300 --> 00:39:45.410
Getting rid of her? Do we have a choice?

00:39:45.410 --> 00:39:48.680
Look, kidnapping is one thing, but murder...

00:39:48.680 --> 00:39:52.720
It wouldn't be murder, more like self-defense.

00:39:52.720 --> 00:39:54.720
It's our next if she gives us away.

00:39:54.720 --> 00:39:56.770
Baby.

00:39:56.770 --> 00:39:59.430
Baby.

00:40:00.350 --> 00:40:02.430
- I've done a lot of foolish things.

00:40:02.430 --> 00:40:03.680
But this is too much.

00:40:15.760 --> 00:40:16.760
- Listen, I gotta talk to--

00:40:16.760 --> 00:40:17.860
- Back on with the muzzle.

00:40:17.860 --> 00:40:19.240
- No, listen!

00:40:19.240 --> 00:40:21.090
- Save your breath, you're gonna need it.

00:40:21.090 --> 00:40:25.650
- I gotta tell you something, it's important.

00:40:25.650 --> 00:40:28.780
- Okay, but it better be damn good.

00:40:28.780 --> 00:40:29.890
- It's gotta be alone.

00:40:31.440 --> 00:40:39.410
- Joe, do you mind? - Well, let's hear it.

00:40:39.410 --> 00:40:41.950
- First of all, I'm not what you think I am. - I know.

00:40:41.950 --> 00:40:44.550
Your Girl Scout work on your badge for the equality of niggers.

00:40:44.550 --> 00:40:46.610
- I'm a government agent. - Oh, yeah?

00:40:46.610 --> 00:40:48.650
Well, I'm Snow White, suffering from a sunburn.

00:40:48.650 --> 00:40:54.850
You're Diana Jackson, age 24, born in Harlem, alias TNT Jackson.

00:40:54.850 --> 00:40:58.570
When you were 13 years old, you were put in a New York State prison for knifing a sailor.

00:40:58.570 --> 00:40:59.670
Shit!

00:41:00.510 --> 00:41:02.580
- You are a lousy, stinking pig.

00:41:02.580 --> 00:41:03.820
Even lower than I thought.

00:41:03.820 --> 00:41:06.200
- I don't care what you think of me.

00:41:06.200 --> 00:41:08.080
What is important is that I need your help.

00:41:08.080 --> 00:41:10.140
- Me, TNT working for the pigs?

00:41:10.140 --> 00:41:10.980
No chance.

00:41:10.980 --> 00:41:12.380
- What if I were able to help you find out

00:41:12.380 --> 00:41:13.340
what happened to Stack?

00:41:13.340 --> 00:41:15.000
- Stack?

00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:17.830
What do you know about him?

00:41:17.830 --> 00:41:20.190
- Trouble outside.

00:41:20.190 --> 00:41:23.720
Charlie and me got the place surrounded.

00:41:23.720 --> 00:41:26.510
What about her?

00:41:26.510 --> 00:41:28.030
- If you say anything to give me away,

00:41:28.030 --> 00:41:30.000
so help me guard all your pig.

00:41:30.120 --> 00:41:32.210
- I'm gonna fall up trying to here. - You got no proof.

00:41:32.210 --> 00:41:33.940
Right now, I got no choice, either.

00:41:33.940 --> 00:41:45.040
What are you doing here, Lance?

00:41:45.040 --> 00:41:47.250
I might ask you the same question, Charlie.

00:41:47.250 --> 00:41:50.390
The shipment got ripped off.

00:41:50.390 --> 00:41:51.640
Today's shipment?

00:41:51.640 --> 00:41:53.940
Right outside the cemetery.

00:41:53.940 --> 00:41:56.400
We feel she has something to do with it.

00:41:56.400 --> 00:41:59.510
I'm sorry, baby.

00:42:00.190 --> 00:42:01.450
- The man wants to see you.

00:42:01.450 --> 00:42:03.150
- You don't really believe that one woman

00:42:03.150 --> 00:42:05.450
could be behind a million dollar drug heist.

00:42:05.450 --> 00:42:09.200
- I had nothing to do with it.

00:42:09.200 --> 00:42:12.720
Ming feels that she was involved,

00:42:12.720 --> 00:42:14.640
so Sid wants to ask you a few questions.

00:42:14.640 --> 00:42:16.380
- Well you go on back to Sid and you tell him

00:42:16.380 --> 00:42:19.630
that TNT spent the afternoon with me.

00:42:19.630 --> 00:42:24.890
- I loved that.

00:42:24.890 --> 00:42:28.740
- Wait a minute, I'll go with you and tell him myself.

00:42:47.920 --> 00:42:57.680
I called the boys off TNT, she and I were together all after the matter.

00:43:00.060 --> 00:43:01.860
I just talked to Max in L.A.

00:43:02.400 --> 00:43:06.390
He's going to get his quota elsewhere unless we come through with something in time.

00:43:06.530 --> 00:43:11.320
I want you to set up another shipment immediately, this time on credit.

00:43:12.150 --> 00:43:15.040
It would be impossible. The arrangement has always been on cash.

00:43:15.240 --> 00:43:19.840
Well, change the arrangement. Just get the shipment through and get TNT.

00:43:19.970 --> 00:43:20.990
I'll do my best.

00:43:21.390 --> 00:43:22.990
What the hell is going on?

00:43:23.190 --> 00:43:27.600
It's about the shipment. I suggest you tell me what happened to it.

00:43:27.710 --> 00:43:28.870
I know nothing.

00:43:31.660 --> 00:43:59.700
- Perhaps you can be persuaded. - Sure, at least, perhaps this would not be necessary.

00:44:00.410 --> 00:44:02.340
I never made it with a chink before.

00:44:02.340 --> 00:44:04.480
Okay, baby.

00:44:17.900 --> 00:44:22.150
You want it, Black? You got it, Black.

00:44:32.750 --> 00:44:33.360
Oh, my God.

00:45:34.540 --> 00:45:40.920
- Doche. - You got a long way to go before you catch up with me.

00:45:41.450 --> 00:45:43.540
'Cause, baby, I was born beautiful.

00:45:43.800 --> 00:45:45.970
I don't know, Charlie. It might be worth the effort.

00:45:49.740 --> 00:45:52.980
- You care to expand on that for me? - All right.

00:45:53.460 --> 00:45:56.500
The heist yesterday was pretty slick.

00:45:57.420 --> 00:45:59.860
You wouldn't be thinking of taking over Sid's spot, would you?

00:46:00.890 --> 00:46:02.350
- Baby, you'll estimate me.

00:46:02.350 --> 00:46:05.800
- Oh no, I don't think I do.

00:46:05.800 --> 00:46:07.410
- Won't you be cool, huh?

00:46:07.410 --> 00:46:09.580
You're putting all kind of ideas in my head.

00:46:09.580 --> 00:46:10.840
- Oh, I'm not saying anything

00:46:10.840 --> 00:46:13.710
that you haven't already thought of, Charlie.

00:46:13.710 --> 00:46:19.930
- Right.

00:46:19.930 --> 00:46:21.420
- What happened to you, man?

00:46:21.420 --> 00:46:24.700
- A slight miscalculation on my part.

00:46:24.700 --> 00:46:27.740
- TNT?

00:46:27.740 --> 00:46:29.190
- You will live to regret this day.

00:46:30.090 --> 00:46:35.920
Ming, I'm going to tell you for the last time, lay off tea.

00:46:35.920 --> 00:46:39.640
I hope I make myself clear.

00:46:39.640 --> 00:46:42.820
I take my orders from Sid, not from you.

00:46:42.820 --> 00:46:44.790
It would be a waste.

00:46:44.790 --> 00:46:49.260
Look, both of you, forget about the black chick.

00:46:49.260 --> 00:46:52.710
We've got more important things to take care of.

00:46:52.710 --> 00:47:00.000
Ming, what about your contacts?

00:47:00.280 --> 00:47:02.690
- They refuse.

00:47:02.690 --> 00:47:03.950
They will not deliver on consignment

00:47:03.950 --> 00:47:05.530
without some sort of guarantee.

00:47:05.530 --> 00:47:07.820
It is for you to make a proposal,

00:47:07.820 --> 00:47:09.830
something that will meet their satisfaction.

00:47:09.830 --> 00:47:12.720
- Well, tell them anything is acceptable to me.

00:47:12.720 --> 00:47:15.660
- Sid, why don't you meet personally with the supplier?

00:47:15.660 --> 00:47:17.000
- This is impossible.

00:47:17.000 --> 00:47:18.440
- Why, Ming, if you're able to meet with him,

00:47:18.440 --> 00:47:19.760
why can't Sid?

00:47:19.760 --> 00:47:22.280
- You do not understand, there are many complications.

00:47:22.280 --> 00:47:24.240
- Ming, we don't have time.

00:47:24.240 --> 00:47:25.720
- I will see what I can do.

00:47:25.720 --> 00:47:27.860
- She up and left.

00:47:27.860 --> 00:47:30.000
Can you imagine, didn't even say goodbye.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.550
Hey, don't even hand me that bullshit, man.

00:47:33.030 --> 00:47:33.970
Now, where is she?

00:47:34.240 --> 00:47:36.920
I'm telling you, man. I don't know.

00:47:37.020 --> 00:47:39.920
And I'm trying to tell you that if Ming gets to her before I do, she's dead.

00:47:40.020 --> 00:47:41.460
Do you understand that?

00:47:41.750 --> 00:47:44.780
Charlie, you know me.

00:47:45.290 --> 00:47:47.000
- If I know, I'd tell you. - Okay.

00:47:48.540 --> 00:47:50.220
Let me put it to you this way.

00:47:51.810 --> 00:47:52.910
Why you...

00:48:01.600 --> 00:48:07.560
And if I don't like what I hear, maybe I'm going to hang my foot up your ass.

00:48:17.050 --> 00:48:20.980
You let her go, I'll kill you.

00:48:22.210 --> 00:48:29.960
Talk to me. Maybe your woman will hurt.

00:49:24.090 --> 00:49:25.030
He is Charlie.

00:49:33.100 --> 00:49:36.630
- Come on, baby, I know you're in there.

00:49:36.630 --> 00:49:39.590
- What do you want?

00:49:39.590 --> 00:49:42.140
- I just wanna make sure you're safe.

00:49:42.140 --> 00:49:44.940
Ming's out to kill you.

00:49:44.940 --> 00:49:47.720
- I know.

00:49:47.720 --> 00:49:50.670
- Yeah, I guess this'll do for the time being.

00:49:50.670 --> 00:49:53.190
- Maybe, but I can't stay here forever.

00:49:53.190 --> 00:49:55.880
I'm already going crazy.

00:49:55.880 --> 00:49:56.840
- You ain't gotta worry about it.

00:49:56.840 --> 00:49:58.070
I have you out here in no time.

00:50:00.320 --> 00:50:03.030
- Come here, let me tell you something.

00:50:03.030 --> 00:50:04.960
Everything's working out beautiful.

00:50:04.960 --> 00:50:06.730
I'm gonna be a big man in this world.

00:50:06.730 --> 00:50:08.480
I'm about to make that move.

00:50:08.480 --> 00:50:10.040
And I want you right there beside me.

00:50:10.040 --> 00:50:10.940
- Oh yeah?

00:50:10.940 --> 00:50:14.030
- Oh yeah, and I'm gonna take care of you.

00:50:14.030 --> 00:50:16.500
Just like I always told you I would.

00:50:16.500 --> 00:50:19.970
- Just what make you so sure that I'm agreeable?

00:50:19.970 --> 00:50:24.960
- You know damn well you're agreeable.

00:50:24.960 --> 00:50:30.000
You'll love it.

00:51:17.340 --> 00:51:23.040
Diana Jackson, age 24, born in Harlem, alias TNT Jackson.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:34.820
- What if I'm an old girlfriend?

00:51:34.820 --> 00:51:41.330
- More like an old enemy, a very old enemy.

00:51:41.330 --> 00:51:44.170
- Diana?

00:51:44.170 --> 00:51:48.580
- I never met the lady.

00:51:48.580 --> 00:51:56.410
Why, are you the jealous type?

00:51:56.410 --> 00:51:59.190
Don't tell me you're backing out on me.

00:51:59.190 --> 00:51:59.790
- No.

00:52:00.480 --> 00:52:02.600
I always stick to my commitments.

00:52:04.190 --> 00:52:12.200
Sid wants to see you. We are moving out.

00:52:12.320 --> 00:52:14.760
- Where? - The Isla del Sol.

00:52:15.510 --> 00:52:18.370
It's a little island just off China's coastal waters.

00:52:18.450 --> 00:52:20.170
It's a Portuguese colony.

00:52:20.450 --> 00:52:22.470
They have a festival going on there.

00:52:23.220 --> 00:52:26.740
If you leave early in the morning, you should arrive late afternoon.

00:52:27.650 --> 00:52:29.700
I'll have to go here. They'll make final arrangements.

00:52:33.130 --> 00:52:35.620
- Angel, this is it.

00:52:35.620 --> 00:52:38.060
It's the opportunity I've been waiting for.

00:52:38.060 --> 00:52:41.490
A chance to meet with the suppliers.

00:52:41.490 --> 00:52:46.750
The whole organization together at once.

00:52:46.750 --> 00:52:52.770
- He's got the light I gave my brother.

00:52:52.770 --> 00:52:56.210
He's the one.

00:52:56.210 --> 00:52:58.000
He murdered Stack.

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:03.580
- Joe, I'm gonna kill his ass.

00:53:03.580 --> 00:53:05.780
- You can count me in.

00:53:05.780 --> 00:53:08.300
- He went to a festival on some island.

00:53:08.300 --> 00:53:12.260
- Isla del Sol.

00:53:41.640 --> 00:53:57.950
There will be nothing to disturb us, as the facilities will be in full swing by then.

00:53:57.950 --> 00:54:00.000
Sid, I'm going out.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:06.310
- Not for a while. What time should I be back? - The meeting is set for 8:00.

00:54:06.310 --> 00:54:08.900
- Okay, I'll be back by then. - Sure, Angel.

00:55:10.360 --> 00:55:12.360
The hotel conference room, eight o'clock.

00:55:12.360 --> 00:55:15.360
Everyone's gonna be there from the pushers to the suppliers.

00:55:15.360 --> 00:55:17.360
So you finally did it.

00:55:17.360 --> 00:55:19.190
Yeah, I finally did it.

00:55:19.190 --> 00:55:21.110
What's the matter? You don't seem too happy about it.

00:55:21.110 --> 00:55:23.110
Oh yeah, I'm happy.

00:55:23.110 --> 00:55:25.090
Come on, this is what you always wanted.

00:55:25.090 --> 00:55:26.090
It's what I thought I wanted.

00:55:26.090 --> 00:55:30.000
I don't know, Gary, sometimes I wonder if I'm not as bad as you.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:37.010
- Yes, they are. - Oh, shit.

00:55:37.010 --> 00:55:45.130
- Diana, we had lost a pig. - You can't butt in now.

00:55:45.130 --> 00:55:48.240
- Well, I gotta do. Can't wait. - We're gonna bust everybody tonight.

00:55:48.240 --> 00:55:50.240
If you interfere, you're gonna blow the whole thing.

00:55:50.240 --> 00:55:52.240
You can figure it out, Charlie. He's all mine.

00:55:52.240 --> 00:56:00.000
- Problem? - Yeah, the black chick. Get rid of him.

00:56:00.060 --> 00:56:01.660
She's going to screw up the whole thing.

00:56:01.660 --> 00:56:02.680
Why?

00:56:02.680 --> 00:56:04.420
Just do it.

00:57:30.730 --> 00:57:32.230
What can I do for you?

00:57:32.230 --> 00:57:34.870
I came to find out about her friend, signor.

00:57:34.870 --> 00:57:36.370
She was arrested a while ago.

00:57:36.370 --> 00:57:37.370
The black girl?

00:57:37.370 --> 00:57:38.190
Yes, sir.

00:57:38.190 --> 00:57:42.610
I just want to know what I can do about getting her out.

00:57:42.610 --> 00:57:45.220
I'm sorry, but I think that's impossible.

00:57:45.220 --> 00:57:50.360
I have orders to keep her in jail under further notice.

00:57:50.360 --> 00:57:53.280
Could I at least talk with her, sir?

00:57:53.280 --> 00:57:54.040
Thank you.

00:58:00.540 --> 00:58:05.830
- Baby. - Joe, I knew you'd be here to get me out.

00:58:06.230 --> 00:58:10.400
- It's not that easy, honey. - Joe, you've got to get me out of here.

00:58:10.400 --> 00:58:19.170
Let's see what I can do. I have to find a way.

00:58:20.370 --> 00:58:22.950
I'll see you tonight, baby. - Joe!

00:59:17.180 --> 00:59:20.900
- What do you think of this one? - Forget it, Angel.

00:59:20.980 --> 00:59:25.120
- You're not going anywhere. - What are you talking about?

00:59:35.720 --> 00:59:37.170
Does this answer your question?

01:00:04.190 --> 01:00:07.110
- What about that? - We'll take care of her after the meeting.

01:00:07.900 --> 01:00:11.520
- Get rid of him. - It's all about Zee.

01:02:22.780 --> 01:02:24.420
They're all here now. We can begin.

01:03:30.410 --> 01:03:46.550
Oh, my God.

01:04:02.940 --> 01:04:04.070
Their minds are made up.

01:04:04.100 --> 01:04:07.240
They do not wish to risk another shipment without payment.

01:04:07.900 --> 01:04:11.300
They say there are many others that are willing to pay cash for their merchandise.

01:04:13.430 --> 01:04:15.860
That's a damn good point.

01:04:16.300 --> 01:04:18.650
Sit down, Charlie. You're not helping matters any.

01:04:18.850 --> 01:04:20.040
I'm not trying to.

01:04:24.050 --> 01:04:25.050
I'll buy from you.

01:04:25.600 --> 01:04:26.600
I got the money.

01:04:27.790 --> 01:04:29.760
To start off with, I want two deliveries.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:31.340
- I'll pay you in cash.

01:04:31.340 --> 01:04:34.430
- You, you ripped off those shipments.

01:04:34.430 --> 01:04:35.910
- That's right.

01:04:35.910 --> 01:04:37.470
- Dirty black bastard.

01:04:42.460 --> 01:04:50.420
- From this day on, you deal directly with me, agreed?

01:04:50.420 --> 01:04:53.720
- I might have something to say about that.

01:04:53.720 --> 01:04:57.910
- My friend, who gives a fuck?

01:05:01.950 --> 01:05:03.400
You're right!

01:05:31.950 --> 01:05:44.660
Ah!

01:06:01.880 --> 01:06:30.000
I don't know you have to say that, right?

01:07:48.400 --> 01:07:56.720
to see you. Everything back there got all screwed up. But now that you're here, what

01:07:56.720 --> 01:08:00.000
the hell did you do that for? The name is Diana Jones.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:05.990
Johnson, TNT to you.

01:11:31.560 --> 01:11:32.020
No!
